Cybersecurity in the Age of AI:
  This was a TED talk hosted by Adi Irani in November 2023, viewed on the 25th of April 2026. The point of this seminar is to iterate just how powerful artificial
  intelligence is, with a focus on how hackers can use it to efficiently create resources such as viruses and phishing emails to steal users' data. It also brought 
  attention to how reliant almost every user is on their private data, and how to protect that data from AI fueled attacks.
  The key defenses are:
    Using generative AI to complete mundane tasks
    Focusing on system design and overall security
    Using AI detectors to check for AI generated content if something looks suspicious
    Do research into how your data can be used against you
